<p>
  <strong>The interim claim.</strong> No transition in 40/40 seeds at
  <span class="mono">mutation_rate ≤ 2<sup>-14</sup></span>, the zero-mutation control
  included, against 5/60 seeds at <span class="mono">≥ 2<sup>-13</sup></span>. No arm
  reaches more than 2 of 10, and the earliest transition anywhere in the sweep is epoch
  9 900. That is the shape a lower edge of a window would have, at a count no arm can yet
  carry.
</p>
<p>
  Four caveats, each of which can still move the reading:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    Every transitioned run's final summary reports
    <span class="mono">replicator_count 0</span>. The detector fires on the
    compression and diversity signature, not on a counted copier — run 45 ends at
    <span class="mono">distinct_tapes</span> 1 935,
    <span class="mono">compress_ratio</span> 0.051,
    <span class="mono">entropy_bits</span> 6.86,
    <span class="mono">copy_rate</span> 6.1 × 10<sup>-5</sup>; run 41 at
    <span class="mono">distinct_tapes</span> 13 349,
    <span class="mono">compress_ratio</span> 0.260,
    <span class="mono">entropy_bits</span> 6.74. So these are transitions in tape
    statistics, not counted self-replicators.
  </li>
  <li>
    Run 41's stored <span class="mono">transition_epoch</span> of 9 900 predates the
    resume fix of PR #25, and its own samples put the collapse near epoch 5 030. It is
    cited as ≤ 9 900 until the backfill of PR #30 lands.
  </li>
  <li>
    Two runs of the <span class="mono">2<sup>-8</sup></span> arm, 99 and 100, were still
    running at the time of the check, so that arm may yet become 2 of 10.
  </li>
  <li>
    Nothing here is readable as a negative result until the
    <span class="mono">bff-control</span> positive control transitions: a flat sweep on an
    untested instrument says nothing about the hypothesis.
  </li>
</ul>
